  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  emails:
  - senderName: staff@aurelianinst.org
    subject: Staff Security Access
    preview: 'Reminder: all active staff badges grant...'
    body: 'Reminder to all Aurelian Institute staff: because of the upcoming gala,
      all active staff badges grant access to every door in the building, including
      collections storage, the security room, and the east wing archive. This was
      implemented to streamline after-hours coverage during the transition period.
      Please report any lost or malfunctioning badges to facilities immediately.'
    timestamp: Yesterday, 3:00 PM
    isUnread: 0
  - senderName: p.sterling@aurelianinst.org
    subject: 're: re: my hours'
    preview: You can't keep cutting my hours and expect me to...
    body: 'You can''t keep cutting my hours and expect me to just go along with it.
      I''ve covered for you more times than I can count this year, late nights, things
      I didn''t ask questions about. That''s worth more than however little you''re
      paying me now.


      We''re talking after the gala whether you like it or
      not.'
    timestamp: Yesterday, 1:30 PM
    isUnread: 0
  - senderName: elaine.harlow@aurelianinst.org
    subject: Tonight, after everyone's gone?
    preview: I know we said we'd wait until...
    body: 'I know we agreed to wait until the weekend, but I don''t think I can get
      through another day without thinking about you. Meet me by my car once Jeremiah
      and the guests clear out. Bring the good wine this time, not whatever you brought
      last week.


      Try not to let it show on your face all night. You''re terrible
      at hiding things.'
    timestamp: Tuesday, 5:15 PM
    isUnread: 0
  - senderName: pruitt@wrenfieldtrust.org
    subject: Midas Grand Timeline Confirmation
    preview: Glad to hear we're moving forward. The board is prepared to...
    body: 'Glad to hear we''re moving forward. The board is prepared to finalize
      the agreement as soon as the collection transfer paperwork is signed on your
      end. Once that''s done, the funding relieves your outstanding obligations immediately,
      and the naming rights are yours as discussed.


      We''ll need staff transition
      plans and a public announcement date. The sooner the better, given your timeline.'
    timestamp: 3:47 PM (one week ago)
    isUnread: 0
  - senderName: d.reyes@reyesfineart.com
    subject: 'Re: Vane Collection Acquisition Agreement'
    preview: I'm following up on your notice that the Institute will no longer...
    body: 'I''m following up on your notice that the Institute will no longer be
      funding further acquisitions from Julian''s studio. Mr. Vane has been informed,
      and he is not taking it lightly.


      He''s been in the studio since yesterday
      morning, ruining paintings that were already finished, going on about "legacy"
      and "betrayal" loud enough that I''ve had two neighboring tenants complain.
      I''ve talked him down twice today alone. I am not equipped to manage a grown
      man having a breakdown. over a business decision that isn''t even mine.


      Whatever
      you two need to sort out, sort it out directly. I''m done being the messenger.'
    timestamp: 10:34 AM (one week ago)
    isUnread: 0
  - senderName: accounts@rossandwhitaker-cpa.com
    subject: "URGENT: Outstanding Balances \u2014 Final Notice"
    preview: This is the third notice regarding the Institute's...
    body: "This is the third notice regarding the Institute's outstanding balances.
      Combined with the loan payments now past due, the Institute is no longer in
      a position to operate as a standalone entity without immediate intervention.
      \n\nAs discussed, folding the collection into a university structure with Pruitt
      may be the only path that avoids formal insolvency proceedings. I'd strongly
      advise finalizing this before your creditors take further action."
    timestamp: 8:02 AM (one week ago)
    isUnread: 0
